What is the output of the following C program?

```c
#include <stdio.h>
int main() {
    int i = 0, j = 0;
    for (i = 0; i < 3; i++)
        for (j = 0; j < 3; j++)
            if (i == j) continue;
            else printf("%d%d ", i, j);
    return 0;
}
```

Consider the following code for a bounded buffer producer-consumer problem using semaphores:

Semaphore empty = n, full = 0, mutex = 1;
Producer:
wait(empty);
wait(mutex);
// produce
signal(mutex);
signal(full);

Consumer:
wait(full);
wait(mutex);
// consume
signal(mutex);
signal(empty);

What would happen if the order of wait(empty) and wait(mutex) were swapped in the producer?
